ure_debugger` may run while the dependency is BLOCKED on it (the one exception to waiting for COMPLETE, recorded in the `operation.ts` lifecycle; a retried dependency is unfinished input again; that debugger runs on a snapshot of the failing candidate, bound to the failed run, and its agent skips the completion oracle entirely (`diagnosticRun`), so neither the configured verifier nor one it discovers after writing a file gates it); a resumed unit is given its current inputs; the `reproduction_command_source` label is derived only together with the command it describes; `authorized_scope` is the operation objective plus the unit's task, which is weaker than a declared file list, and a `replace_task` decision records the scope change (`scopeChange`); a `reproduction_command` is trusted only when operator-configured, otherwise labelled untrusted; caller `inputs` override; anything it cannot derive fails closed naming the input. Tests: `cli/test/specialist_contract_enforcement.test.ts`, `cli/test/specialist_auto_inputs.test.ts` (through `AgentWorkUnitExecutor.run` and `/team`). The verdict-gate clause is WITHDRAWN: `isReviewRole` already covers `reviewer` and `acceptance_reviewer`; `security_reviewer` has no verdict contract and gets the structured-result gate. |
